cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use SafeUnfollow in your work, please cite it as below.'
title: SafeUnfollow
abstract: 'Find out who unfollowed you on Instagram. SafeUnfollow reads the official Instagram data export and computes unfollowers, non-mutuals and mutuals entirely in the browser; the export never leaves the device. No login, no server, no Instagram API.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Romanov
    given-names: Ignat
identifiers:
  # The concept DOI, and deliberately only that one: it resolves to whichever
  # version is newest, so it cannot go stale. Zenodo also mints a DOI per version
  # (10.5281/zenodo.22663616 for 1.6.0), and that one would be wrong the moment
  # 1.7.0 ships while still reading as current — nothing in this repository
  # updates it, and the release that would falsify it is the release nobody
  # rechecks this file during.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22663615
    description: 'Concept DOI — always resolves to the latest archived version.'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ignromanov/safe-unfollow'
url: 'https://safeunfollow.app'
license: MIT
version: 1.6.0
date-released: '2026-09-08'
keywords:
  - instagram
  - unfollow
  - tracker
  - privacy
  - local
  - react
  - typescript
  - open-source
  - data-analysis
  - social-media
